Implement user story SKY-002-B: Vitest test suite for SkyscannerClient

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests covering constructor validation, fetch request construction, successful response parsing, HTTP error handling, malformed response handling, and mock mode behavior. All tests mock global fetch — no real network calls.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts contains vitest tests using mocked fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) with afterEach fetch restoration, covering: (a) correct RapidAPI URL and header construction, (b) successful response parsed into FlightResult[], (c) HTTP 4xx rejection with status code in error message, (d) missing/empty API key constructor error, (e) malformed/missing-fields response body rejects with parse/validation error
- client.test.ts includes a test verifying MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns deterministic fixture data without invoking fetch (spy/stub on global fetch, assert never called)
- client.test.ts includes tests verifying MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API set to non-'true' values (empty string, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') still performs the real fetch call — mock mode is strict opt-in, not a fuzzy truthy check
- vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- Class SkyscannerClient constructor accepts object with optional apiKey property: constructor({ apiKey }: { apiKey?: string } = {})
- Constructor throws Error with exact message: 'Skyscanner API key is required. Provide apiKey in constructor or set RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable.' when apiKey is missing, undefined, or empty string
- Constructor falls back to process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY when apiKey not provided: const providedKey = apiKey ?? process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- Mock mode is triggered ONLY when process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (strict string equality, not truthy)
- In mock mode, returns copy of MOCK_FLIGHT_RESULTS array: return [...MOCK_FLIGHT_RESULTS]
- MOCK_FLIGHT_RESULTS contains 3 flights with prices 120, 250, 95 USD respectively
- Real API call uses URL: https://skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com/search with query params origin, destination, date, and optional adults
- API request headers: 'X-RapidAPI-Key': this.#apiKey, 'X-RapidAPI-Host': 'skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com'
- HTTP error thrown with message: `HTTP error: ${response.status} ${response.statusText}` when !response.ok
- Response validation: throws Error('Invalid API response: missing Itineraries array') when data.Itineraries is missing or not an array
- Response validation: throws Error('Invalid API response: missing OutboundLeg in Itinerary') when itinerary.OutboundLeg is missing
- All errors are wrapped and re-thrown with prefix 'Flight search failed: ' via catch block
- Standalone searchFlights function exists: export async function searchFlights(params: SearchParams, options?: { apiKey?: string }): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- No validation on adults parameter - accepts 0, negative numbers, or any integer
- No validation on origin/destination format - accepts any string
- No validation on date format - accepts any string
- Currency defaults to 'USD' when data.Currencies is missing or empty

## Mock Strategy
